# apps-to-close.txt.example
# List of applications to close automatically
#
# Format: One app per line, using one of three methods:
#
# 1. APP_NAME: Standard app name (use for most apps)
#    Example: ChatGPT
#
# 2. PATH:/path/to/app: Full path (for apps with generic process names)
#    Example: PATH:/Applications/Visual Studio Code.app
#    Required for: VS Code (appears as "Electron"), IntelliJ (appears as "idea")
#
# 3. FORCE:bundle.identifier.pattern: Force quit using pkill (for stubborn apps)
#    Example: FORCE:com.devexperts.tos.ui.user.thinkorswim
#    Required for: Java apps that ignore graceful quit
#
# Comments start with #
# Blank lines are ignored

# Standard apps (close by name)
ChatGPT
Google Chrome
Microsoft Edge
Microsoft OneNote
Microsoft Outlook
Messages
Slack
Stickies
GitKraken
Quicken
Docker Desktop
iTerm2

# Apps with problematic process names (close by path)
PATH:/Applications/Visual Studio Code.app
PATH:/Applications/IntelliJ IDEA Ultimate.app
PATH:/Applications/DataGrip.app
PATH:/Applications/Microsoft Teams.app
PATH:/Applications/Sublime Text.app

# Stubborn apps requiring force termination (close by bundle ID)
FORCE:com.devexperts.tos.ui.user.thinkorswim
